  "description": "This exceedingly simple garlic-and-herb butter comes together in minutes—and instantly upgrades vegetables, chicken, bread, pasta, and more.",
  "notes": "Notes: To make escargot butter by hand, finely chop garlic, shallot, and parsley leaves. In a medium bowl, combine garlic, shallot, parsley, salt, and a crack of black pepper. Add cubed butter and, using a wooden spoon or flexible spatula, mix until well-combined. Refrigerate in an airtight container.\n\nMake-ahead and storage: Escargot butter can be refrigerated in an airtight container for up to 14 days or frozen for up to 1 month. Thaw overnight in refrigerator before using.",
